{"step_index":3489,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-29T00:18:23Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-29T05:48:23+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-29T05:48:23+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/app.js`\nTotal Lines: 2010\nTotal Bytes: 84058\nShowing lines 815 to 915\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n815:   renderArea1Code(step, currentSubstep) {\n816:     this.codeLinesContainer.innerHTML = \"\";\n817:     let activeRowEl = null;\n818: \n819:     const cond = step.condition;\n820:     const isConditionStep = step.eventType === \"CONDITION\";\n821: \n822:     this.traceResult.rawLines.forEach((rawLine, idx) => {\n823:       const lineNum = idx + 1;\n824:       const isCurrent = step.line === lineNum;\n825: \n826:       // Phase 3: Highlight the branch that executes / is skipped\n827:       let branchBadge = \"\";\n828:       if (isConditionStep && cond) {\n829:         const isBranchLine = lineNum === step.line + 1;\n830:         if (isBranchLine) {\n831:           branchBadge = cond.result\n832:             ? `<span class=\"branch-badge is-executes\">✓ executes</span>`\n833:             : `<span class=\"branch-badge is-skipped\">✗ skipped</span>`;\n834:         }\n835:       }\n836: \n837:       const row = document.createElement(\"div\");\n838:       row.className = `code-row ${isCurrent ? \"is-current-line\" : \"is-dimmed\"}`;\n839:       if (isCurrent) {\n840:         activeRowEl = row;\n841:       }\n842: \n843:       const pointerHTML = isCurrent ? `<span class=\"code-gutter-pointer\">▶</span>` : \"\";\n844:       row.innerHTML = `\n845:         <div class=\"code-gutter\">${pointerHTML}<span>${lineNum}</span></div>\n846:         <div class=\"code-syntax\">${this.highlightPythonSyntax(rawLine)}${branchBadge}</div>\n847:       `;\n848: \n849:       row.addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n850:         const targetIdx = this.traceResult.steps.findIndex((s) => s.line === lineNum);\n851:         if (targetIdx !== -1) {\n852:           this.stopAutoPlay();\n853:           this.goToStep(targetIdx, 0);\n854:         }\n855:       });\n856: \n857:       this.codeLinesContainer.appendChild(row);\n858:     });\n859: \n860:     // Keep the active line centered inside the scrollable code box on mobile/tablet\n861:     if (activeRowEl && this.codeLinesContainer.scrollHeight > this.codeLinesContainer.clientHeight) {\n862:       const container = this.codeLinesContainer;\n863:       const targetTop =\n864:         activeRowEl.offsetTop - container.offsetTop - container.clientHeight / 2 + activeRowEl.clientHeight / 2;\n865:       container.scrollTo({ top: Math.max(0, targetTop), behavior: \"smooth\" });\n866:     }\n867:   }\n868: \n869:   highlightPythonSyntax(line) {\n870:     if (!line) return \" \";\n871:     let commentPart = \"\";\n872:     let codePart = line;\n873:     const hashIdx = line.indexOf(\"#\");\n874:     if (hashIdx !== -1) {\n875:       codePart = line.slice(0, hashIdx);\n876:       commentPart = `<span class=\"syn-com\">${this.escapeHTML(line.slice(hashIdx))}</span>`;\n877:     }\n878: \n879:     const tokenRegex = /(\".*?\"|'.*?'|\\b(?:class|def|return|if|elif|else|for|while|in|break|continue|and|or|not|True|False|None|self)\\b|\\b(?:print|range|len|min|max|abs|sum|list|int|float|str|bool|round|enumerate|sorted|reversed|set|dict)\\b|\\b\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?\\b)/g;\n880:     const highlighted = this.escapeHTML(codePart).replace(tokenRegex, (match) => {\n881:       if (match.startsWith('\"') || match.startsWith(\"'\")) {\n882:         return `<span class=\"syn-str\">${match}</span>`;\n883:       }\n884:       if (/^(class|def|return|if|elif|else|for|while|in|break|continue|and|or|not|True|False|None|self)$/.test(match)) {\n885:         return `<span class=\"syn-kw\">${match}</span>`;\n886:       }\n887:       if (/^(print|range|len|min|max|abs|sum|list|int|float|str|bool|round|enumerate|sorted|reversed|set|dict)$/.test(match)) {\n888:         return `<span class=\"syn-bi\">${match}</span>`;\n889:       }\n890:       if (/^\\d/.test(match)) {\n891:         return `<span class=\"syn-num\">${match}</span>`;\n892:       }\n893:       return match;\n894:     });\n895: \n896:     return highlighted + commentPart;\n897:   }\n898: \n899:   /* =========================================================\n900:      AREA 2: TEACHING AREA, QUICK ITERATION BAR & THONNY STEPPER\n901:      ========================================================= */\n902:   renderArea2Teaching(step, currentSubstep) {\n903:     const lesson = currentSubstep || step.teacherLesson;\n904: \n905:     // Render Quick Iteration / Phase Pills Bar\n906:     this.renderQuickIterationBar();\n907: \n908:     this.teachStepTitle.textContent = lesson.title || step.teacherLesson.title;\n909:     this.teachCodeBox.innerHTML = this.highlightPythonSyntax(lesson.codeSnippet || step.codeText);\n910: \n911:     // Phase 4: Interactive Learning Prediction Card (Optional)\n912:     this.renderInteractivePredictCard(step, currentSubstep);\n913: \n914:     // Phase 3: Loop Return Indicator & Loop Array Pointer Tracker\n915:     this.renderLoopReturnBanner(step, currentSubstep);\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":3490,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-29T00:18:23Z","input_tokens":2079,"cache_read_tokens":271185,"output_tokens":4536,"thinking":"The code renders a line of code, applying different classes based on whether it is the currently active line. If it's active, it retrieves a focused snippet and highlights it. The HTML of this highlighted line is then constructed.\n\n\nExamining the scenarios for `getActiveFocusSnippet` reveals its core logic. The function determines the snippet to highlight based on the `currentSubstep`'s context within a larger `step`. This could include directly using a provided snippet from `currentSubstep.codeSnippet` if available, or extracting a relevant section from the raw line based on condition evaluation. The presence of a focused snippet then influences the rendering of both the line itself and a teaching code box.\n\n\nThe function's behavior depends on the nature of the highlighted snippet. If a complex expression (like a function call or arithmetic operation) is present, the entire expression will be highlighted within the code box. For assignments, the assigned value or variable itself is highlighted. Loops show the loop variable or the range.\n\nIf the active snippet is the same as the entire line of code, the system must highlight the specific variable or value. For assignments, this would be the value being assigned or the variable being assigned to. This applies to return statements and conditional statements as well.\n\n\nFocusing on the snippet extraction logic, the code prioritizes `exprFrames` to extract the relevant snippet. If `exprFrames` are unavailable, it checks `currentSubstep.codeSnippet`, after trimming leading/trailing characters and removing `if` statements. The snippet matching considers array bracket expressions as well.\n\n\nThe function determines the highlighted snippet based on the current step's type, prioritizing direct matches. Conditional expressions are highlighted directly if present. For augmented assignments, it checks for operation details to highlight the right-hand side or target variable. Assignment operations highlight the assigned value or the variable being assigned. Loop iterations focus on the loop variable or range.\n\n\nAnalyzing different event types to extract the active snippet. For loop iterations, the loop variable or iterable expression is identified if present in the raw line. Conditional statements directly highlight their expressions. Return statements prioritize the return value string, then attempts to capture the returned expression using a regex. Function calls are handled by matching the function name with captured arguments. Printing events focus on the content within the print call. Function definitions use the function name or a regex to extract the defined function name.\n\n\nThe active snippet highlighting is now examined with a sample input, tracing its behavior through string slicing and HTML generation. The CSS changes in `:root`, `.code-view`, `.code-gutter`, and `.code-row.is-current-line` related to background, border, font, and shadow are inspected. It appears the changes affect background and border colours of code blocks.\n\n\nThe provided CSS rules define the visual styling for different code elements. The `.code-row.is-current-line` and `.code-gutter` styles manage the appearance of the currently active line, including background, border, and highlighting, indicating focus. The `.thonny-token-box` rules create a distinct visual representation for tokens, highlighting with a border, background, and pop-in animation. Finally, `.teach-code-box` specifies the font, size, weight, and background color for the teaching code box.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/styles.css","EndLine":25,"StartLine":1,"toolAction":"Viewing root CSS variables","toolSummary":"Check root variables in styles.css"}}]}
